+/*
+ * alp-sdk (Alp Lab AB): fullLinesStd/fullLines/fps/maxIntLine/minAgain/
+ * maxAgain below are OV5647 facts, not this reference table's generic
+ * placeholders -- see alp-sdk's isp_pico.c (isp_apply_ae()'s header
+ * comment) for the exact derivation (pixel_rate 58333333 Hz, HTS(640x480
+ * binned) 1852; AGC_GAIN 0x350a is 10-bit, register 0x10 = 1x).
+ *
+ * UPDATED (bench run 81): fps, fullLinesStd/fullLines and maxIntLine now
+ * target 10 fps, not 15 -- the library's own microseconds-to-lines
+ * conversion for isp_ae_param.int_time_max evidently uses THIS static
+ * table internally,
+ * independent of whatever int_time_max (microseconds) isp_apply_ae()
+ * supplies at runtime: run 81 measured the AE loop capped at exactly 2095
+ * lines (this table's OLD 15 fps maxIntLine) even after isp_apply_ae()
+ * derived a 10-fps-based ceiling from video_get_frmival(). VTS at 10 fps =
+ * pixel_rate / (hts * frmrate) = 58333333 / (1852 * 10) = 3149
+ * (ov5647_frmrate_to_vts()'s own integer-truncating formula, ov5647.c);
+ * maxIntLine = VTS - 4 = 3145. alp-sdk's examples/aen/aen-isp-ov5647-
+ * capture now runs the sensor at 10 fps (OV5647's floor rate) by design,
+ * so this table tracks that, not the sensor's power-on-default 15 fps.
+ * If int_time_max ever needs to vary at RUNTIME with an app-chosen frame
+ * rate beyond what this static table encodes, that is a real library-
+ * level gap this patch does not close -- documented, not fixed here.
+ *
+ * UPDATED (bench run 83): maxDgain was 0x1FF (511). dgain shares aGain's
+ * scale (1024 = 1x -- see isp_api_wrapper.c's totalGain = aGain * dGain /
+ * ISP_SNS_GAIN_ACCU, ISP_SNS_GAIN_ACCU = 1024), so a maxDgain of 511 is a
+ * ceiling of ~0.5x -- HALF of unity gain, not a generous headroom figure.
+ * Advisor root cause, arithmetic-confirmed: with maxAgain 65472 (its own
+ * correct ceiling) and dgain capped under 1x, isp_apply_ae()'s own
+ * dgain_min/dgain_max = 1024 (unity, isp_pico.c) get silently clamped
+ * DOWN to this table's lower maxDgain by the library's own attribute
+ * validation, capping the ACHIEVABLE total gain (aGain * dGain / 1024)
+ * at roughly half of aGain alone -- bench run 83's gain register 0x1fd
+ * (509, ~31.8x) sitting well under aGain's own ceiling equivalent
+ * (65472 * 16 / 1024 = 1023 = the sensor's full register range) matches
+ * this exactly (509 =~ 1023 * 511 / 1024). Set to 1024 (unity, matching
+ * isp_apply_ae()'s own intent: all headroom flows through again, dgain
+ * pinned) so the library's floor no longer silently overrides what the
+ * app-facing struct isp_ae_param asked for.
+ *
+ * UPDATED (bench run 85): minDgain was 64 (~0.0625x) -- NOT the binding
+ * constraint for run 83's bug (that was maxDgain, above), but at the AE
+ * floor (dark scene, gain driven all the way down) the library was free to
+ * pick anywhere in [minDgain, maxDgain], and it picked near the floor:
+ * sensor gain register read back 0x01 (~1/16x) even with isp_apply_ae()'s
+ * own dgain_min/dgain_max = 1024 (unity, isp_pico.c) -- the SAME "app asked
+ * for unity, library's own attribute table let it go lower" pattern as run
+ * 83's maxDgain bug, just at the other end of the range. Pinned to 1024
+ * (== maxDgain) so dgain is unity always, matching isp_apply_ae()'s intent:
+ * all headroom flows through again alone.
+ *
+ * aeTarget now reads CONFIG_VIDEO_ISP_VSI_AE_TARGET (zephyr/kconfigs/
+ * vendor-alif-peripherals.kconfig) -- the SAME Kconfig isp_apply_ae()
+ * (isp_pico.c) reads for its own struct isp_ae_param.ae_target, so the
+ * two literals (this file's compile-time default and isp_pico.c's
+ * runtime-applied value) cannot drift out of sync the way two independent
+ * `= 50` literals could. Bench run 81/83: an ae_target of 50 (mid-grey)
+ * was unreachable in the bench's dark lab even at the AE loop's own
+ * exposure/gain ceiling; the Kconfig's own default stays 50 (a sane
+ * production starting point) -- lower it via a build-time overlay to
+ * diagnose reachability, not by editing this literal.
+ *
+ * maxDgain/minDgain/dgainStep/aeRunInterval/dampOver/dampUnder/tolerance/
+ * initExposure/aeMode/gainThreshold (aeTarget now excepted, above) are
+ * left at this file's own defaults -- algorithm tuning constants, not
+ * sensor register facts, expect a bench pass.
+ */
